message: >-
  If you use Folklore Clinical Variant Interpretation MCP, please cite this
  software using the metadata below.
title: Folklore Clinical Variant Interpretation MCP
type: software
authors:
  - name: Helena Bioinformatics
    website: https://helena.bio
version: 1.7.0
date-released: 2026-10-31
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.23849196
url: https://folklore.helena.bio
repository-code: https://github.com/helena-bioinformatics/folklore-mcp
license: Apache-2.0
keywords:
  - clinical variant interpretation
  - genomics
  - bioinformatics
  - ACMG/AMP
  - Model Context Protocol
  - germline variants
abstract: >-
  The official public Model Context Protocol adapter for Folklore by Helena
  Bioinformatics. It provides automated ACMG/AMP germline variant classification
  and assessment, criterion-level evidence, source provenance, gene profiles,
  ClinGen gene-disease associations and literature. Public API clients support
  variant identity resolution, immutable gene profile snapshots and separate
  live literature captures.
references:
  - type: generic
    title: Public germline variant interpretation contract benchmark
    url: https://github.com/helena-bioinformatics/folklore-mcp/tree/main/benchmarks/variant-interpretation
  - type: generic
    title: Neutral comparison method for automated ACMG/AMP tools
